  "sourceTitle": "Glazed Apple Cookies",
  "sourceText": "Glazed Apple Cookies\nBy: Anonymous\nPublished: Sunday, December 13, 2009 - 12:46am\n\nIngredients\n\n\n\n\n2 cups sifted flour\n1 teaspoon baking soda\n1/2 cup shortening\n cups brown sugar (packed)\n1/2 teaspoon salt\n1 teaspoon cinnamon\n1/4 cup apple juice or milk\n1 teaspoon ground cloves\n1/2 teaspoon nutmeg\n1 egg (unbeaten)\n1 cup nuts\n1 cup apples, chopped\n1 cup raisins\n1/2 - 1 c. powdered sugar\n1/2 teaspoon vanilla\n2 1/2 teaspoons milk\n1 tablespoon butter\n1/8 teaspoon salt\n\nPreparation\n\n1 For apple juice cook apple peelings in small amount of water. Mix all the above well and bake, 400 degrees, 10-15 minutes. 2 Mix well and put glaze on cookies while they are warm from the oven.",
